<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Damascus</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1924 CE · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the states into which France divided Syria in 1920, built around Damascus and later merged into a unified Syrian state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arab-kingdom-of-syria">Arab Kingdom of Syria</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maysalun">Maysalun</a> in July 1920, the French high commissioner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-gouraud">Henri Gouraud</a> divided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> into several states to weaken Arab nationalism. The State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, created in September 1920, covered Damascus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hama">Hama</a> and the south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state had a local government under a governor, the first being <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haqqi-al-azm">Haqqi al-Azm</a>, with French advisers holding real authority. It was the centre of nationalist politics and resentment at the division of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>. In 1922 it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-federation">Syrian Federation</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-aleppo">State of Aleppo</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alawite-state">Alawite State</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the end of 1924 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> dissolved the federation and merged the states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-syria">State of Syria</a>, which took effect in January 1925.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-damascus.jpg" alt="State of Damascus" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Damascus.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1924 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Haqqi al-Azm</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Syria</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Damascus State</dd></dl></aside></div>
